From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:59:45 +0900
Subject: Forget a parenthesized type's elements once it is not a parameter
 list
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`Parsers.typ` records, for each type it reads inside parentheses, whether it is
an erased parameter, in case the parentheses turn out to be the parameter list
of a function type. If they do not — no arrow follows — it goes on to read the
rest of the type with those entries still recorded. Should that type then turn
out to be the single parameter of a function type after all, as in

    (A & B)^ ?=> T

where the capture set comes between the parentheses and the arrow, one more
entry was added for it, and `FunctionWithMods` was built with one parameter and
two entries: an AssertionError out of the parser, with no diagnostic. With
capture checking off, `^` is not read as part of the type and the same source
gets an ordinary syntax error.

The entries are now dropped when the parentheses are found not to be a
parameter list. None of them can be `true` there: an erased element sends the
parser down the function path.

Upstream no longer has the buffer (0114fb812f6, "Simplify erased parameters"),
so this is needed only before that.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code); reviewed content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: parenarrow
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/parsing/Parsers.scala  |  4 ++++
 .../captures/paren-capturing-arrow.scala             | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/pos-custom-args/captures/paren-capturing-arrow.scala

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/parsing/Parsers.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/parsing/Parsers.scala
index 875ac7cc461feb6517e213dfb71a64d622418f50..680cfdc2b621205ca49a438a35340774c60cc774 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/parsing/Parsers.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/parsing/Parsers.scala
@@ -1842,6 +1842,10 @@ object Parsers {
           if in.isArrow || isPureArrow || erasedArgs.contains(true) then
             functionRest(args)
           else
+            // The parenthesized types are not a function's parameters after all, so
+            // what was recorded for each as one does not describe the parameter
+            // that the whole type may yet turn out to be, as in `(A & B)^ => C`.
+            erasedArgs.clear()
             val tuple = atSpan(start):
               makeTupleOrParens(args.mapConserve(convertToElem))
             typeRest:
diff --git a/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/paren-capturing-arrow.scala b/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/paren-capturing-arrow.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b9117749a4fb9b2a51e68382187d1f6e051672f3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/paren-capturing-arrow.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+// A parenthesized type with a capture set, as the parameter of a function type. The
+// types within the parentheses were counted as parameters of a function, and the
+// whole type then counted again as the one parameter it is.
+
+trait A
+trait B
+
+def context[T](block: (A & B)^ ?=> T): T = ???
+def impure[T](block: (A & B)^ => T): T = ???
+def pure[T](block: (A & B)^ -> T): T = ???
+type F[T] = (A & B)^ ?=> T
+type G[T] = ((A & B)^) ?=> T
